; An allocation the runtime cannot have is a runtime error: the report
; locates the form that asked for it (exit 5). The golden runs with
; NEXIS_MAX_ALLOC=16777216, which refuses any one block past 16 MiB, so
; the typed vector below, one block of 8 bytes an element, fails as its
; elements pass 16 MiB instead of exhausting the machine.

(defn fill [n]
  (count (i64-vector (repeat n 0))))

(println "before")
(fill 100000000)
(println "never")
